## Caveats

- S∈{7,8,16,32} are intentionally not included — the chain recursion circuit at current `main` panics with "Failed to build circuit" for `tx_per_proof > 6`. Tracked in issue #8 (one-line `log_gates=15` fix not yet landed). When #8 lands, rerun this toolkit with the extended sweep.
- Build flag is `RUSTFLAGS="-C target-cpu=native"`, so per-shape numbers reflect the best the local CPU can deliver and are **not** directly comparable to cross-compiled or generic-x86_64 builds.
- All numbers are from a **single run per (shape, S)**. No averaging across repeats. Treat ±5% as noise.
- Build time is excluded from `wall_s` (build wall is captured separately in `machine-info.txt` per shape).
